AB  - There has been a growing prevalence of AI adoption in the workplace primarily aimed at enhancing performance and productivity. However, knowledge of how such adoption potentially impacts employee well-being is still limited and fragmented. To address this gap, we conduct a systematic review of 74 articles on AI and well-being to take stock of the current literature. Our review synthesizes the types of AI, well-being outcomes, theoretical perspectives, and methodological approaches in the current literature, showing that AI adoption presents both opportunities and challenges for employees' psychological, social, and physical well-being and identifying major theoretical frameworks concerning the influence of AI adoption on well-being. Drawing on the ability-motivation-opportunity (AMO) model, we develop a comprehensive, evidence-based framework for leaders and organizations to integrate AI into HR practices that enhance employees' abilities, motivations, and opportunities to perform, while safeguarding employee well-being. We conclude by discussing the implications for future research and practice.
